raw.opening_A:
{
"explanation": "A Selvar contraction first looks for an eligible edge using only the structure of the input graph. An edge qualifies if it is a bridge, so that removing it disconnects the graph. An edge also qualifies if it lies on an induced cycle of length exactly four, meaning a square with no chord. Longer chordless cycles, such as pentagons, do not qualify on their own, and neither do triangles. If any edge qualifies, pick one and contract it once. Merge its endpoints, delete any self-loop, and collapse duplicate edges. The result is not tested again. If no edge qualifies, the operation is undefined. Under this rule a path has only bridges, so it is defined. A chordless four-cycle is defined through its square. A chordless five-cycle has no bridge and no induced four-cycle, so it is undefined.",
